# Rocci CLI reference

**Status:** current.

This page documents the `rocci` binary only. `rocdown` and [okmate](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate) are
other products; see [Rocdown CLI](/docs/rocdown/cli/).

Examples use a source checkout. Until a distribution exists, the spelling is
`cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- …`. An installed `rocci` would drop the Cargo
prefix.

## Validate

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- validate [rocci.toml]
```

Parse and validate configuration. Unknown fields and unsafe hosts are errors.
Default path `rocci.toml`. Exit non-zero on failure.

## Build

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- build INPUT [-o OUTPUT]
```

Lower one `.rocci` file to Roc. `-o` writes a file; otherwise stdout.

## Build WASI HTTP module (experimental)

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- build --http-module INPUT.rocci [-o http-module.wasm]
```

Writes a hello-web WASI guest (`wasi:http`-shaped exports), **not** apply
`--host wasm` and **not** a musl `--release` process. `rocci run` stays native
0.16. The `.rocci` path is required for the CLI shape; the bytes today are the
linked hello-web fixture, not a compiled app.

## Build release

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- build --release INPUT [-o OUTPUT] [--target x64musl|arm64musl]
```

Package a Linux **server** plus `assets/` (not a macOS `.app`). `INPUT` may be
an app directory, a standalone `.rocci`, or `rocci.toml`. `--target` requires
`--release`.

## Run

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run [ENTRY] [serve options]
```

Standalone directory (`rocci run .` or `rocci run <dir>`), standalone
`.rocci` file, or custom directory/`main.roc`. A standalone directory
resolves a unique entry (`[app].entry`, then unique `@init` / `@context`,
then unique `@get:view("/")`, then a single `.rocci`). Two process inits
in one tree fail. Bare `rocci run` still defaults to `main.roc`. Starts
HTTP and opens a preview window by default. Extra args after the entry go
to the Roc binary.

## View

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view INPUT --component NAME [--arg name=val]
```

Preview one component. HTTP declarations are ignored. `--component Hello` and
`--component hello` both work.

## Browse

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- browse [ROOTS…]
```

Component gallery.

## Playground

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- playground INPUT [--mode wasm|local]
```

`--mode wasm` (default) runs in a worker and does not snapshot HTML.
`--mode local` can snapshot through native Roc.

The public site hosts the same WASM workbench at `/playground/`. It lowers source to generated Roc and AST; HTML preview is not available there.

## Render

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- render INPUT [--fragment] [-o OUTPUT]
```

`Html.render` snapshot. `--fragment` skips the document wrapper.

## Inspect

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- inspect INPUT [--ast]
```

Components, fixtures, styles, handlers, generated Roc, and source-map
segments. Segments always print; there is no `--segments` flag. `--ast` adds
the S-expression tree.

## Ast

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- ast INPUT
```

Parse tree only.

## Test

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- test [PATH]
```

Compile each `.rocci` file (or each `.rocci` under a directory; default `.`)
that declares `@test`, stage a type module with an `expect` trailer, and run
`roc test` on that module. Files without tests are skipped (exit 0). Rocci
diagnostics or a failing `roc test` exit non-zero.

## Bundle

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- bundle [--config rocci.toml] [--target …]
```

Ad-hoc signed macOS `.app`. Host-native; `--target` is rejected for `.app`.
`--target` on this command is for Linux process binaries in other flows.
Production signing is planned.

## Datastar

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- datastar pin VERSION [--app PATH]
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- datastar update [--app PATH]
```

Pin or upgrade the Datastar JS asset. `run` does not auto-upgrade.

## Serve options

Shared by `run`, `view`, `browse`, and `playground`:

| Option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--no-window` | off | Serve without the preview window |
| `--no-live-reload` | off | Pause automatic refresh; watch still rebuilds |
| `--log-handlers` | off | Log matched handlers to stderr / Dev Console |
| `-v` / `--verbose` | off | Per-module template timings, listen heartbeats, and Roc `--timings` / `--verbose` from `roc build --opt=dev`. Phase start/done lines always print. |
| `--port PORT\|auto` | `auto` with a window; `8000` with `--no-window` | Also `ROC_BASIC_WEBSERVER_PORT` |

**Related:** [Configuration](/docs/reference/configuration/), [Install](/docs/install/).
